{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTVandermondeKeystone","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Roots","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Polynomial.Vieta","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.BigOperators","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Field"],"declarations":32,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaLagrange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.betaLagrange","kind":"theorem","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L292-L312","doc":"**The β-Lagrange identity.** For distinct nodes `β : Fin k → ℚ` (`k ≥ 1`),\n\n∑ᵢ βᵢ · ∏_{j≠i}(βᵢ − 1 − βⱼ)/(βᵢ − βⱼ)  =  (∑ⱼ βⱼ) − C(k,2).\n\nThe self-contained `ℚ` partial-fractions identity the GNW hook-summation identity reduces to. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prod_erase_eq_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prod_erase_eq_neg","kind":"theorem","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L284-L290","doc":"Removing the `j = i` factor from `∏ⱼ(βᵢ − 1 − βⱼ)` flips a sign (that factor is `βᵢ−1−βᵢ = −1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.residPoly_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.residPoly_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L249-L282","doc":"**(Vieta, residual leading coefficient — proved.)** `R.coeff (k−1) = C(k,2) − ∑ⱼ βⱼ`.  This was the\nlast open step of the β-Lagrange identity; the whole cone is now sorry-free.\n\nFor `k ≥ 2`, `R.coeff (k−1) = shiftPoly.coeff (k−2) − nodePoly.coeff (k−2) + k·nodePoly.coeff (k−1)`\n(`coeff_X_mul`/`coeff_C_mul`); by Vieta the two `coeff (k−2)` are `e₂(β+1)`/`e₂(β)`, whose difference is\n`esymm2_shift`; with `nodePoly.coeff (k−1) = −∑β` the result is `(k−1)∑β + C(k,2) − k∑β = C(k,2) − ∑β`.\n`k = 1` is the direct `R.coeff 0 = −β₀ = C(1,2) − β₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prodLin_coeff_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prodLin_coeff_2","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L242-L247","doc":"**Vieta at index `k−2`.** `[Xᵏ⁻²] ∏ⱼ(X − fⱼ) = e₂(f)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.esymm2_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.esymm2_shift","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L233-L240","doc":"**The `e₂` shift.** `e₂(β+1) − e₂(β) = (k−1)·∑β + C(k,2)`, via the `powersetCard 2` definition of\n`esymm` (`esymm_map_val`), `pair_diff` per `2`-subset, and `sum_pairs_eval`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.pair_diff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.pair_diff","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L227-L231","doc":"On a `2`-element set, `∏(βᵢ+1) − ∏βᵢ = (∑βᵢ) + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.sum_pairs_eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.sum_pairs_eval","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L209-L225","doc":"`∑_{t : 2-subset} (∑_{i∈t} βᵢ + 1) = (k−1)·∑β + C(k,2)` — the double-count: each element lies in\n`k−1` of the `2`-subsets, and there are `C(k,2)` of them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.count_pairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.count_pairs","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L179-L207","doc":"The number of `2`-subsets of `Fin k` containing a fixed element is `k − 1` (bijection with the\nother element, `j ↦ {i, j}` over `univ.erase i`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.residPoly_natDegree_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.residPoly_natDegree_lt","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L150-L175","doc":"**(Vieta, residual degree)** The residual has degree `< k`: the `Xᵏ⁺¹` and `Xᵏ` coefficients of\n`G` and `(X − C k)·Q` cancel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.shiftPoly_coeff_gt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.shiftPoly_coeff_gt","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L147-L148","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.shiftPoly_coeff_k","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.shiftPoly_coeff_k","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L146-L146","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.shiftPoly_coeff_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.shiftPoly_coeff_top","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L142-L145","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.nodePoly_coeff_gt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.nodePoly_coeff_gt","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L140-L141","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.nodePoly_coeff_k","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.nodePoly_coeff_k","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L139-L139","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.nodePoly_coeff_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.nodePoly_coeff_top","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L137-L138","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.sum_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.sum_shift","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L131-L133","doc":"`∑ⱼ (βⱼ + 1) = (∑ⱼ βⱼ) + k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prodLin_coeff_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prodLin_coeff_top","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L124-L129","doc":"**Vieta top coefficient.** `[Xᵏ⁻¹] ∏ⱼ(X − fⱼ) = −∑ⱼ fⱼ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prodLin_coeff_gt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prodLin_coeff_gt","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L119-L122","doc":"Coefficients strictly above `k` vanish. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prodLin_coeff_k","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prodLin_coeff_k","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L114-L117","doc":"The `Xᵏ` coefficient is `1` (monic of degree `k`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prodLin_natDegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prodLin_natDegree","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L109-L112","doc":"`∏ⱼ (X − fⱼ)` has degree `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prodLin_monic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prodLin_monic","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L105-L107","doc":"`∏ⱼ (X − fⱼ)` is monic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.nodes_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.nodes_card","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L101-L103","doc":"The node multiset has cardinality `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prodLin_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.prodLin_eq","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L94-L99","doc":"`∏ⱼ (X − fⱼ)` as a product over the node multiset, for Vieta. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.esymm_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.esymm_one","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L88-L92","doc":"`esymm s 1 = s.sum` (the singletons are the cardinality-`1` subsets). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.bigPoly_eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.bigPoly_eval","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L75-L84","doc":"Value of `G` at a node: `G(βᵢ) = βᵢ · ∏ⱼ(βᵢ − 1 − βⱼ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.bigPoly_decomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.bigPoly_decomp","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L71-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.residPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.residPoly","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L67-L69","doc":"The residual `R = G − (X − C k)·Q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.bigPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.bigPoly","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L64-L65","doc":"`G(X) = X · ∏ⱼ (X − (βⱼ+1))`: at a node, `G(βᵢ) = βᵢ · ∏ⱼ(βᵢ − 1 − βⱼ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.shiftPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.shiftPoly","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L60-L62","doc":"The shifted-node polynomial `∏ⱼ (X − (βⱼ+1))`, whose value at `βᵢ` is `∏ⱼ(βᵢ − 1 − βⱼ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.sum_eval_div_eq_of_decomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.sum_eval_div_eq_of_decomp","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L46-L58","doc":"**Decomposition reduction.** If `G = R + H·Q` with `deg R < k`, then `∑ᵢ G(βᵢ)/Dᵢ = R.coeff (k−1)`:\n`Q` kills the `H·Q` part at every node, and the keystone evaluates the `R` part. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.nodePoly_eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.nodePoly_eval","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L39-L44","doc":"`Q` vanishes at every node `βᵢ` (the `j = i` factor is `βᵢ − βᵢ = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.nodePoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaLagrange.nodePoly","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaLagrange.lean#L35-L37","doc":"`Q(X) = ∏ⱼ (X − βⱼ)` — the node polynomial. It vanishes at every node. ","signatureChunk":0}]}